{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotFactorSpectralDerivation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotFactorSpectralDerivation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.knotFactor_of_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.knotFactor_of_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorSpectralDerivation.lean#L102-L114","doc":"**Normalisation.**  If both expansions are those of the identity\n(`χ_λ(𝟙) = d_λ` on every block, `d_λ ≠ 0`), the knot factor is the\ntotal weight `Σ_λ w_λ`.  With `w_λ = τ(e_λ)` that total is\n`τ(𝟙) = 1`.  The old weights `dim_q² V_λ / [n]_q!` fail this, which\nis the defect the 2026-11-16 restatement removes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.knotFactor_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.knotFactor_self","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorSpectralDerivation.lean#L85-L100","doc":"**Self-pairing.**  Pairing a braid with itself gives the Plancherel\nsum of squared character ratios,\n\n  `a_K(β, β) = Σ_λ w_λ · (χ_λ(β) / χ_λ(𝟙))²` ,\n\nthe \"sum of positive squares\" form.  Over an ordered field every\nsummand with `w_λ ≥ 0` is non-negative, which is what makes the\namphicheiral corollary's sign flip on the alternating block\nobservable rather than a convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.knot_factor_spectral_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.knot_factor_spectral_form","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorSpectralDerivation.lean#L67-L83","doc":"Unfolding lemma for `knotFactor` (true by definition; it is the\nrewrite rule `KnotFactorAmphicheiral` uses).  The mathematical\ncontent of the narrative identity, the evaluation\n`τ(π(β) β*) = Σ_λ w_λ χ_λ(β) χ_λ(β*) / d_λ²`, is proved in the\n`.md` from orthogonality of the central idempotents; it is not\nencoded here, because `HeckeExpansion` carries no algebra. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:knot-factor-spectral-form","label":"prop:knot-factor-spectral-form","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-factor-spectral-derivation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.knotFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.knotFactor","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorSpectralDerivation.lean#L61-L65","doc":"The knot-factor `a_K` as a Gram pairing on the chirality block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion.trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion.trivial","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorSpectralDerivation.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion.weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion.weight","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorSpectralDerivation.lean#L58-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion.c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion.c","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorSpectralDerivation.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion.partitions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion.partitions","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorSpectralDerivation.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion.mk","kind":"ctor","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorSpectralDerivation.lean#L55-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion","kind":"structure","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorSpectralDerivation.lean#L52-L59","doc":"Central-idempotent character expansion of a braid in `H_n(q)`,\nover the Hecke base ring `R` (§7c: generic; `R := ℚ(q)` is the\nintended instance, `R := ℝ` the archimedean one). ","signatureChunk":0}]}